# vfs_bind_file: a single FILE mounted at a name of its own -- how the
# generated `z` unit's z/project.z is the user's real project.z.
# `{ROOT}` is template-substituted by the test runner.
#
# Coverage:
#   - register fs on a file answers a FILE root dentry (1), not a panic
#   - bind of that file under a directory of another provider makes no
#     mount: the walk at the name answers the file itself (1)
#   - the bound file opens, and reads its path from where it was bound
#   - its provider path is the file's own name
#   - a sibling in the directory it was bound into is unaffected
#   - a walk under a file answers notfound
#   - open on a mount reads as a directory rather than panicking
vfs register fs {ROOT} gen
vfs register fs {ROOT} proj/project.txt
vfs stat 1
vfs walk 0 z
vfs bind 2 project.txt 1 instead
vfs walk 2 project.txt
vfs stat 1
vfs open 1
vfs path 1
vfs pathfromprovider 1
vfs walk 2 build.txt
vfs open 3
vfs walk 1 nested
vfs stat 4
vfs bindroot 0 before
vfs open 5
